Suggests: konsole
Description: crash notifications with a one-click AI diagnosis
 When a program crashes, Lili Crash lets you know, and with one click asks an
 AI coding assistant such as Claude Code or Codex to investigate and explain
 what happened. It also notices a computer that froze, a Steam game that
 closes right after starting and an app that won't open. On KDE Plasma a tray
 icon shows the crash history and the assistants' usage limits. After
 installing, each user runs "lili-crash setup" once.
